Having less turns to BUC ID doesn't really give you extra
survivability.  Yes, the AC you get from armor might be better than
some of the other classes, since you'll be more likely to BUC ID every
piece of armor in the mines, but that is about all priests have to
offer.

Priests don't get a guaranteed good melee option like some of the
other classes (e.g. knights and valkeries can easily get excalibur
early in the game), and they don't get guaranteed good spell options
like some of the other classes (wizards, monks, and healers).  Priests
also don't get a decent ranged option (yes, they get polearms, but
unlike knights, they don't get automatic #jump, automatic speed, and
automatic extra bonus speed from a mount -- meaning that the polearms
aren't terribly exciting for priests).  Priests also don't get any
useful class-dependent intrinsics until you are so far into the game
that you don't really need them anymore.

Priests basically don't get an "oh crud" option if something scary
happens.  Cavemen at least get to multi-shot a massive stack of rocks
as an "oh crud" option.


